\title{perturbdyngen: Paired Perturb-seq Simulation of Gene Regulatory Networks}
\description{
Simulates knockdown (CRISPRi) and activation (CRISPRa) Perturb-seq screens on dyngen gene regulatory network models. Wild-type and perturbed cells are simulated as coupled pairs with common random numbers, so genes upstream of a perturbation are unchanged by construction. A guide UMI layer and an RNA capture layer (shared library size, negative binomial counts) turn molecule counts into Perturb-seq-like observations. Includes a network sampler (log-normal degrees, burn-in scaffolding, reachability repair), experiment designs, the networks and configuration files of the CausalODE benchmark, and AnnData export.
